  "id": "congo_portobelo",
  "name": "Congo (Afro-Panamanian Costa Arriba drum-song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Congo is the drum-song and dance-drama tradition of the Afro-Panamanian communities of the Costa Arriba of Colón, centred on Portobelo, whose people descend from enslaved and maroon Africans. In the Carnival season Congo groups re-enact the struggle against slavery in plays with devil figures (diablos), while women lead the songs in call-and-response with a chorus over drums and hand-clapping. UNESCO has inscribed the ritual and festive expressions of the Congo culture on its Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage. The membrane-drum and hand-drum cards stand in for the Congo drums.",
